# Restore point before stopping

`CONTINUE.md` is the handoff file. A new Cursor login or chat has no old memory. Read `CONTINUE.md` first, then resume from **Do next**. Do not restart finished work or a new 3-epoch Colab train unless that file says to.

When the user says credits/limit are ending, when a long task is only partly done, or before you stop, **update `CONTINUE.md` in the same turn** (do not only say it in chat):

- What happened and what was decided
- Files already changed
- Exact next steps (numbered)
- What not to do

Chat transcripts are optional. The project file is the source of truth so a new ID can say: `CONTINUE.md padho aur wahi se chalo`.
